dnf install iperf3 numactl kernel-tools sysstat

iperf3 ≥ 3.16 (multi-threaded) is the main tool
numactl for NUMA/CPU pinning
mpstat / sar for CPU monitoring

2. What to Measure (Baseline vs After Tuning)
Run the exact same tests before and after applying the playbook.

#  Single stream  #  Per-flow performance (often CPU limited)  #  iperf3 -c <peer> -t 30 -i 5
# Multi-stream   #   Maximum aggregate throughput   #   iperf3 -c <peer> -P 8 -t 30 -i 5
#  Reverse   # Receive performance   #   Add -R
#   Bidirectional   #  Full-duplex   #  Add --bidir
#   CPU usage    #   Whether CPU is the bottleneck   #   Run mpstat -P ALL 1 in another terminal
#  Drops / errors  #   Whether buffers/interrupts are healthy   #   ethtool -S <iface> | grep -E 'drop|error|miss|disc'

3. Recommended Test Procedure
A. Before any tuning (Baseline)
Note current settings:

ethtool -g <iface>
ethtool -c <iface>
sysctl net.core.rmem_max net.core.wmem_max net.ipv4.tcp_congestion_control
tuned-adm active
cat /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_governor

Run these tests (record the SUM line):

# Single stream
iperf3 -c <PEER_IP> -t 30 -i 5

# 8 parallel streams (most important for 100G)
iperf3 -c <PEER_IP> -P 8 -t 30 -i 5

# Reverse (server → client)
iperf3 -c <PEER_IP> -P 8 -t 30 -i 5 -R

# Optional: bidirectional
iperf3 -c <PEER_IP> -P 4 -t 30 -i 5 --bidir

While tests are running, watch:
mpstat -P ALL 1
ethtool -S <iface> | grep -E 'drop|error|miss|disc'

B. Apply the Ansible playbook
C. After tuning – repeat the exact same tests
4. Tips for Reliable 100G Results

Use a recent iperf3 (≥ 3.16) so multi-stream is properly multi-threaded.
Prefer pinning to the correct NUMA node when possible:
# Find NUMA node of the NIC
cat /sys/class/net/<iface>/device/numa_node

# Example: run iperf3 on cores of that node
numactl -N <numa_node> iperf3 -c <PEER_IP> -P 8 -t 30
Run tests for at least 20–30 seconds (the first few seconds are ramp-up).
Test both directions and note CPU usage on both ends.
Expect roughly:
Single stream: often 15–40 Gbit/s (CPU core limited)
8 streams: 80–95+ Gbit/s is a good result on a well-tuned 100G path


